# =============================================================================
# .env.example — the CANONICAL environment matrix for the whole SaaS (ADR-0002)
# =============================================================================
# Copy to `.env` for local runs (infra/compose reads it; keep it chmod 0600).
# Real values NEVER go in this file — placeholders are `changeme` / `localhost`.
#
# RULES (spec §4 conventions + §15.2 app security):
#   * Canonical names come from the Zod schemas in `packages/config/src/env/`
#     (gateway.ts / worker.ts / engine-pool.ts / web.ts). A REQUIRED var that
#     is missing, invalid or still `changeme` makes the process REFUSE TO
#     START — fail fast, §4: "missing var = process refuses to start".
#     Secrets are NEVER silently defaulted.
#   * A handful of transport/dev knobs are parsed at the app boundary instead
#     (gateway src/env.ts, worker src/env.ts, apps/web src/lib/env.ts,
#     @studio/storage, @studio/billing guardrails); each row says who parses
#     it. Adding a variable means touching this file AND the parser in the
#     same change (ADR-0002). App code never reads `process.env` directly.
#   * Rows marked `# future:` exist only as policy placeholders — NOTHING
#     parses them yet. Do not rely on them until a schema adopts them.
#   * Secrets live only in env files / the secret store — never in the repo,
#     never in logs (§15.2), separate keys per environment (§17.5). See
#     docs/secrets-policy.md for storage, rotation and incident protocol.
#
# Environments (§17.5): local | staging | production.
#   local     — infra/compose on the dev machine, mock engine, test keys.
#   staging   — SAME box, SEPARATE Compose project (COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME) +
#               subdomain + separate DB + Stripe TEST keys. Never test
#               migrations on production first (§17.5).
#   production— the Lightsail box (§17.1); live keys only.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# INSIDE COMPOSE vs ON THE HOST — read before editing any hostname below
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The canonical .env is read by BOTH the containers (env_file) and Compose
# interpolation (infra/compose, --env-file ../../.env). Inside the Compose
# bridge network the services address each other by SERVICE NAME:
#   db:5432          — PostgreSQL 16 (compose service `db`)
#   valkey:6379      — Valkey 8 (compose service `valkey`; BullMQ owns DB 0,
#                      GlitchTip's cache uses DB 1)
#   gateway:8787      — REST + SSE API (metrics listener 3001, internal only)
#   worker:9876       — worker ops endpoint (/health + /metrics, internal only)
#   engine-pool:3002  — engine session supervisor (internal only)
#   web:3000          — Next.js SSR/app origin
# So on the box DATABASE_URL / VALKEY_URL / GLITCHTIP_DATABASE_URL /
# GLITCHTIP_REDIS_URL use the db:/valkey: hostnames (values below). On the
# host (local dev WITHOUT compose) use localhost:5432 / localhost:6379 plus
# the dev port bindings in infra/compose/docker-compose.override.yml.example
# — and keep the password in DATABASE_URL in sync with POSTGRES_PASSWORD.
# Staging: same file shape, own copy (e.g. /srv/studio-staging.env) +
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=staging — see infra/environments.md (§17.5).
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Core / shared (all apps)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Deployment environment: local | staging | production (§17.5) — the selector
# docs, deploy scripts and secret separation key on. Not yet a packages/config
# schema row (flagged to the config owner); apps derive behavior from NODE_ENV.
APP_ENV=local
# Runtime mode for frameworks: development | test | production. Parsed by every
# @studio/config schema (default development); worker src/env.ts mirrors it.
NODE_ENV=development
# Canonical public URL of the WEB app (links, emails, OAuth redirects).
# Parsed by the gateway + web schemas; the gateway also uses it as the CSRF /
# trustedOrigins allowlist entry for cookie mutations (§15.2 — allowlist only
# the app domain, never *). In prod: https://<APP_DOMAIN>.
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Public DNS name the box serves (REQUIRED on the box): Caddy site address +
# ACME certificate ({$APP_DOMAIN} in infra/caddy/Caddyfile); DNS must exist
# before first boot or ACME fails (§17.1 first-boot runbook). Interpolated by
# infra/compose — keep `localhost` for pure local runs.
APP_DOMAIN=localhost
# Email for ACME expiry notices (OPTIONAL): add it to the Caddyfile's global
# `email` block too — an empty value is a Caddy config error, so leave unset
# if you do not want notices. Interpolated by infra/caddy.
# ACME_EMAIL=ops@example.com
# Internal upstreams Caddy proxies to — compose service names by default
# ({$GATEWAY_INTERNAL}/{$WEB_INTERNAL} in the Caddyfile); override only if the
# apps run off-box. Interpolated by infra/compose + infra/caddy.
GATEWAY_INTERNAL=gateway:8787
WEB_INTERNAL=web:3000
# Log level floor: trace | debug | info | warn | error (gateway transport +
# worker src/env.ts; @studio/agent's logger honors it too, §22 — prompts are
# redacted unless the workspace opts in).
LOG_LEVEL=info

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gateway (apps/gateway — Hono REST + SSE + webhooks, spec §13)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Listen port. The @studio/config schema calls it PORT (PaaS-style, default
# 3001); the gateway transport projection (src/env.ts) accepts GATEWAY_PORT
# first and falls back to PORT. Compose + Caddy pin 8787 — keep that on the box.
GATEWAY_PORT=8787
# Better Auth session/cookie signing key (REQUIRED, gateway schema `AUTH_SECRET`)
# — 32+ random bytes, e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`. SESSION-COOKIE NOTE: the
# session cookie is signed with this secret and is httpOnly + secure +
# sameSite per §15.2; its name is the library default. There is NO separate
# SESSION_COOKIE* variable — the old BETTER_AUTH_SECRET name is dead.
AUTH_SECRET=changeme
# Base URL where Better Auth handlers are mounted (OAuth / magic-link
# callbacks resolve against it) — the GATEWAY origin. Parsed by
# apps/gateway/src/auth/server.ts (local projection of the schema env).
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:8787
# Gateway origin for server-side calls: REST + SSE base (web schema calls it
# API_BASE_URL; see the Web section for the browser-side NEXT_PUBLIC_ twin).
# Engine-pool control URL for the deep health probe (§13.1). OPTIONAL gateway
# schema row (http URL); compose service name inside the bridge network.
ENGINE_POOL_URL=http://engine-pool:3002
# Service version stamped into logs / health payloads (gateway src/env.ts;
# defaults to the npm package version). Local override knob — on the box the
# deploy scripts pin image tags instead.
SERVICE_VERSION=0.1.0

# --- SSE tuning (§13.1–13.2: backfill from run_events, then live; resume via
#     Last-Event-ID; client dedupes by seq). Gateway schema rows. -------------

# Milliseconds between SSE keep-alive heartbeats on GET /v1/runs/:id/events.
SSE_HEARTBEAT_MS=15000
# Milliseconds the server tells a reconnected client to wait before retrying.
SSE_RETRY_MS=3000
# Max events replayed from run_events when a stream connects (backfill first).
SSE_BACKFILL_LIMIT=500

# --- Gateway-local knobs (parsed in apps/gateway, NOT yet config rows) ------

# Comma-separated deep-health probe flags (GET /v1/health/deep, §13.1):
# db,valkey,storage,engine_pool,providers — unset = report zero dependencies.
# Parsed by apps/gateway/src/routes/health.ts.
# GATEWAY_HEALTH_PROBES=db,valkey
# Directory holding templates/ and components/ manifests (gateway catalog);
# unset = the repo's built-in catalog dir. Parsed by
# apps/gateway/src/services/catalog.ts (strict: an EMPTY value refuses boot).
# STUDIO_CATALOG_DIR=./catalog

# future: UPLOAD_MAX_FILE_BYTES / UPLOAD_MAX_FILES_PER_REQUEST and the
# RATE_LIMIT_* knobs (auth/runs/uploads/exports) below are §15.2 policy
# constants in code today (apps/gateway RATE_LIMIT_PRESETS + §15.2 caps) —
# nothing parses env for them yet. Adopt in @studio/config when tunables land.
# UPLOAD_MAX_FILE_BYTES=26214400
# UPLOAD_MAX_FILES_PER_REQUEST=10
# RATE_LIMIT_AUTH_PER_MINUTE=10
# RATE_LIMIT_RUNS_PER_MINUTE_PER_WORKSPACE=6
# RATE_LIMIT_UPLOADS_PER_HOUR_PER_USER=20
# RATE_LIMIT_EXPORTS_PER_MINUTE_PER_WORKSPACE=10

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Worker (apps/worker — BullMQ: agent loop, critic, exports)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Concurrent jobs per worker process across all queues (split evenly over the
# queue set); 2 replicas × small concurrency on the 4 GB box (§17.2). Parsed
# by apps/worker/src/env.ts (1–64, default 8).
WORKER_CONCURRENCY=4
# Ops endpoint port: GET /health + Prometheus /metrics (src/health.ts +
# src/metrics.ts). INTERNAL compose bridge only — never a published port.
WORKER_HEALTH_PORT=9876
# Bind address for the ops listener. Loopback by default; compose sets
# 0.0.0.0 so Prometheus (obs profile) can scrape across the bridge — still
# box-private (§17.2 only Caddy publishes host ports).
WORKER_HEALTH_HOST=127.0.0.1

# --- Engine binding (local dev; parsed by apps/worker/src/processor.ts) -----
# MOCK_ENGINE=1 (|true|yes) forces the mock-engine adapter so local dev boots
# without a Rust build. Otherwise the binding follows ENGINE_BINARY_PATH: a
# present binary selects the engine-pool path; a missing one downgrades to
# the mock. Production MUST ship the real binary (§3.2).
# MOCK_ENGINE=1
# Connect to an ALREADY-RUNNING mock engine instead of spawning one per
# session: port + its 64-hex control token (both required together).
# MOCK_ENGINE_PORT=0
# MOCK_ENGINE_TOKEN=<64-hex token>
# mock-engine-internal (apps/mock-engine; usually spawned with these set —
# set by hand only when running it directly): write root for doc.save /
# doc.render (MOCK_ENGINE_WRITE_ROOT) and chaos hooks MOCK_FAULT=
# crash-on-command|hang|oversized-reply. Never enable in production.

# future: per-queue retry/retention knobs — BullMQ attempts, the §14.2 daily
# cap multiplier and §15.3 retention windows are constants/config today.
# WORKER_MAX_JOB_ATTEMPTS=3
# BILLING_DAILY_CAP_MULTIPLIER=2
# RETENTION_AGENT_STEPS_DAYS=90

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Engine pool (apps/engine-pool — one engine process per tenant session, §3.2)
# (the ENGINE_* rows below are parsed by BOTH the worker and engine-pool
#  @studio/config schemas; the caps rows are engine-pool-only)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Internal control-API port of the supervisor itself (engine-pool schema PORT,
# default 3002). Gateway reaches it via ENGINE_POOL_URL; never published.
# PORT=3002
# Absolute path to the pinned engine binary `photocraft-cli` (ADR-0001) —
# required, never defaulted (§4). In compose the host dir /engine is bind-
# mounted read-only and the image pins ENGINE_BINARY_PATH=/engine/photocraft-
# cli: NEVER override this away from /engine in the box .env (W9-I decision).
ENGINE_BINARY_PATH=/home/z/my-project/vendor/photocraft/target/release/photocraft-cli
# Root directory under which per-workspace capability roots are created
# (§3.2 capability scoping; compose uses the engine_work volume → /work).
ENGINE_CAPABILITY_ROOT_BASE=/home/z/my-project/studio/.local/engine-work
# Timeouts per §3.4: tool 5 s, render 30 s, run 10 min, session idle 15 min.
ENGINE_TOOL_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
ENGINE_RENDER_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
ENGINE_RUN_TIMEOUT_MS=600000
ENGINE_SESSION_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=900000
# Connections per engine session — mirrors vendor automation/src/security.rs.
ENGINE_SESSION_MAX_CONNECTIONS=16
# Memory watchdog limit per engine session (MB); the pool dies before the box
# starves (§17.4). CPU shares stay a compose resource limit, not env.
ENGINE_SESSION_MEM_LIMIT_MB=2048
# Global pool ceiling on this box; per-plan session caps live in code (§14.1).
ENGINE_POOL_MAX_SESSIONS=32

# Engine-process env (PHOTOCRAFT_CONTROL_TOKEN, PHOTOCRAFT_CONTROL_TOKEN_FILE,
# PHOTOCRAFT_AUTOMATION_READ_ROOT, PHOTOCRAFT_AUTOMATION_WRITE_ROOT) is set
# per session BY THE SPAWNER (apps/engine-pool/src/spawners) — never in .env.

# future: pool warm-keep / session lifetime recycling (min-idle, max-lifetime)
# are not parsed anywhere yet; start small and scale per §17.4 triggers.
# ENGINE_POOL_MIN_IDLE_SESSIONS=0
# ENGINE_SESSION_MAX_LIFETIME_SECS=7200

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fonts (§1.5 constraint 9 — NEVER commit font files)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Root of the pinned craft-fonts clone (ADR-0001). The engine-pool spawner
# merges CRAFT_FONTS_DIR into every engine spawn env; fonts are read from here
# at build / render time. Font binaries in this repo are a review-blocker.
CRAFT_FONTS_DIR=/home/z/my-project/vendor/craft-fonts

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web (apps/web — Next.js marketing + product UI)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Next.js server port (web schema calls it PORT, default 3000; the compose
# healthcheck reads WEB_PORT — keep the two names' values in sync).
WEB_PORT=3000
# Gateway REST + SSE base for SERVER-SIDE calls (web schema API_BASE_URL).
API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787
# Browser-visible gateway base INCLUDING the /v1 prefix (§13). Inlined into
# the client bundle by next.config.ts (envPrefix NEXT_PUBLIC_) and parsed by
# apps/web/src/lib/env.ts — client env is public by definition: NEVER put a
# secret in a NEXT_PUBLIC_* var.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787/v1
# Browser-visible app origin (optional twin of APP_URL; parsed when present so
# typos still fail fast).
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Gateway origin serving /api/auth/* — the Better Auth client base (W8-B
# contract var, apps/web/src/lib/auth.ts). Falls back to NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_
# URL minus /v1 when unset; set it whenever auth moves off the API origin.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_URL=http://localhost:8787
# Realtime presence transport selector: centrifugo | sse | off (unset = sse,
# §3.1 "SSE first"). Parsed by apps/web/src/lib/realtime/presence.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_REALTIME=sse
# Centrifugo WS/HTTP endpoint (REQUIRED only when NEXT_PUBLIC_REALTIME=
# centrifugo; Centrifugo is optional at start, §13.2).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CENTRIFUGO_URL=wss://rt.example.com

# future: PUBLIC_WEB_URL from earlier drafts — superseded by APP_URL +
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL; nothing parses it. Do not set.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Infra — Postgres (§12 data model, Drizzle; source of truth, §3.1)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Connection string (REQUIRED by the gateway/worker/engine-pool schemas).
# INSIDE COMPOSE the hostname is the service name `db` (see the hostname
# block at the top); on the host use localhost:5432. The password MUST match
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD below (the compose `db` service is initialized from it).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://studio:changeme@db:5432/studio
# Postgres superuser password for the compose `db` service (REQUIRED — compose
# fails fast without it, §4; no secret defaults). MUST match DATABASE_URL.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme
# Postgres role + database created on first boot (compose interpolation).
POSTGRES_USER=studio
POSTGRES_DB=studio
# One-shot migrations run `docker compose run --rm --no-deps -e MIGRATE=1
# gateway` — MIGRATE is a run-time flag for the image entrypoint, NOT an
# env-file row (W9-J contract). Local → staging → prod, always in that order.
# future: DATABASE_POOL_MAX / DATABASE_SSL are not parsed yet — packages/db
# pins pool max 10 / TLS off and defers to DATABASE_URL query params today.
# DATABASE_POOL_MAX=10
# DATABASE_SSL=false

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Infra — Valkey (BullMQ queues, rate-limit counters, SSE presence)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Valkey connection URL (REQUIRED by the gateway/worker schemas; optional for
# the engine-pool). Valkey, NOT Redis 7.4+ (license policy §16.5) — the URL
# scheme is the standard RESP `redis://` wire scheme, the HOST is the compose
# service `valkey`. INSIDE COMPOSE use the hostname `valkey`; on the host use
# localhost:6379 (see the hostname block at the top).
VALKEY_URL=redis://valkey:6379

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Infra — Object storage (§3.1 objects; driver selected by @studio/storage)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Driver selector: local | s3 (REQUIRED by createStorageFromEnv — no silent
# default; an unset driver fails fast rather than quietly using local disk
# in production). local = local dev; s3 = Cloudflare R2 in prod (§17.1).
STORAGE_DRIVER=local
# local driver (REQUIRED when STORAGE_DRIVER=local): writable base dir, a
# signing secret for local signed URLs (>= 16 random chars) and the public
# base URL the signed URLs resolve against (e.g. the gateway origin).
STORAGE_LOCAL_DIR=/home/z/my-project/studio/.local/storage
STORAGE_SIGNING_SECRET=changeme16-pluschars
STORAGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787
# S3/R2 sixtuple (REQUIRED by the gateway/worker schemas AND the s3 driver;
# S3_ENDPOINT must be a valid http(s) URL — AWS: https://s3.<region>.
# amazonaws.com; R2/MinIO: custom). Bucket keys are workspace/<id>/… (§15.1).
S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
S3_REGION=auto
S3_BUCKET=changeme-assets
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=changeme
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=changeme
# Optional s3 extras (@studio/storage): key prefix (ends with "/") and R2
# compatibility quirks flag ("true"/"1").
# S3_PREFIX=
# S3_FORCE_R2_COMPAT=true
# Versioned backups bucket for infra/scripts/backup.sh pg_dump targets
# (§17.1 backups row; + S3_BACKUP_PREFIX in the script headers).
S3_BACKUP_BUCKET=changeme-backups
# future: S3_SIGNED_URL_TTL_SECS / S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE are not parsed —
# signed-URL lifetime is code policy (<= 900 s, §15.1) and R2 quirks are
# handled by S3_FORCE_R2_COMPAT today.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Infra — Stripe (§14 credits, plans and billing)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secret API key (REQUIRED, gateway schema) — must match sk_test_… / sk_live_…;
# TEST keys for local + staging (§17.5), live keys for production only.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=changeme
# Webhook signing secret (REQUIRED, gateway schema, must match whsec_…) —
# signature verification is mandatory and idempotent by event id (§15.2, §14.3).
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=changeme
# Publishable key (REQUIRED, web schema — billing pages; pk_test_… / pk_live_…).
# Safe for the browser; the secret scope stays server-side (§14.3).
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=changeme
# Five recurring/one-time price ids (§14.1), read from the raw env by
# apps/gateway/src/services/stripe.ts + billing-complete/wiring-check.ts (NOT
# yet @studio/config rows). Production refuses to start on the NoopStripe
# seam with these unset (§4 fail-fast, wiring-check).
STRIPE_PRICE_STARTER=changeme
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO=changeme
STRIPE_PRICE_MAX=changeme
STRIPE_PRICE_PACK=changeme
STRIPE_PRICE_EXTRA_SEAT=changeme
# Legacy aliases (still honored): STRIPE_PRICE_PLAN_100_CREDITS (=STARTER),
# STRIPE_PRICE_PLAN_250_CREDITS (=PRO), STRIPE_PRICE_PLAN_120_CREDITS (=MAX),
# STRIPE_PRICE_CREDIT_PACK_100 (=PACK). Prefer the five names above.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Infra — Model providers (routing table §5.3) — PAID-ONLY
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# §1.5 constraint 6: customer content must NEVER flow through free / training
# LLM tiers (free tiers train on data). No OpenRouter in production. Request
# `store:false` / no-training flags where the provider offers them (§15.3).
# All five keys are OPTIONAL @studio/config rows BY DESIGN: the worker boots
# without any provider (queue housekeeping still works) and the health map
# (`modelProviderHealth()`, packages/config worker.ts) reports each class as
# configured / unconfigured — a run whose tier needs an UNCONFIGURED class is
# REFUSED, never silently rerouted. Circuit breakers fail over to the
# alternate same-class provider (§5.3, §17.4). Prod tiers: gemini = default
# planner/executor/critic; anthropic = premium/max (Sonnet/Opus classes);
# openai = HD image finals; deepseek = economy (paid tier, off-peak batch);
# flux = image drafts (host below).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

GEMINI_API_KEY=changeme
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=changeme
OPENAI_API_KEY=changeme
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=changeme
FLUX_API_KEY=changeme
# Base URL of the paid image-drafts host serving Flux 2 Schnell drafts
# (optional, http URL; HD finals go through gemini/openai above).
# FLUX_BASE_URL=changeme
# Per-model rate overrides for the cost meter (§5.2/§18.2 — every call is
# metered and attributable). JSON over the built-in table; garbage FAILS
# FAST (MeteringError). Parsed by packages/agent/src/metering/cost-model.ts.
# MODEL_RATES_JSON={"gemini-2.5-flash":{"kind":"text","inputUsdPerM":0.30,"outputUsdPerM":2.50}}
# future: GOOGLE_VERTEX_PROJECT / GOOGLE_VERTEX_REGION / GOOGLE_VERTEX_CLIENT_
# EMAIL / GOOGLE_VERTEX_PRIVATE_KEY (the Workload-Identity prod path for the
# gemini class) are NOT parsed — the worker schema takes GEMINI_API_KEY
# today. Adopt via @studio/config before switching the default class to
# Vertex. Same for per-request AI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS / AI_PROVIDER_MAX_RETRIES
# (timeouts/retries are §5.3 code policy today).

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Guardrails (kill switches — @studio/billing guardrails, §18.4 / §21 drills)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Global kill switch for the shared demo account flow: false | 0 | off | no
# disables it platform-wide (default enabled). Parsed by
# packages/billing/src/guardrails/demo-workspace.ts (§16.2/§18.4).
DEMO_ENABLED=true
# Comma-separated provider-class kill switch (§21 drill `PROVIDERS_DISABLED=
# anthropic` drains the vendor before maintenance/outage): empty = all live.
# Parsed by packages/billing/src/guardrails/provider-killswitch.ts.
# PROVIDERS_DISABLED=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Observability (§22)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OTLP HTTP endpoint for OpenTelemetry traces/metrics (optional, all app
# schemas; collector on the box). Spans: HTTP → queue → worker → tool → engine.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318
# Trace sampling floors (@studio/agent obs/tracer.ts): successes ~10%, errors
# ALWAYS kept (raise, never lower the error floor). Plain decimals.
OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLING_RATE=0.1
OTEL_TRACES_ERROR_SAMPLING_RATE=1
# future: OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL (http/protobuf keeps the box agentless
# and light) is not parsed yet — the tracer default is the only behavior.
# GlitchTip DSN — Sentry-compatible error ingestion (optional client row in
# all app schemas; free cloud tier or self-host on-box, §17.1).
GLITCHTIP_DSN=changeme
# --- GlitchTip SERVER (compose profile "obs" only; the DSN above is the
#     client). GlitchTip MUST use its OWN database + role on the shared
#     Postgres — never the app DB — and Valkey DB 1 (BullMQ owns DB 0).
#     Create the role/DB once: see the glitchtip block in infra/compose.
GLITCHTIP_SECRET_KEY=changeme
GLITCHTIP_DATABASE_URL=postgres://glitchtip:changeme@db:5432/glitchtip
GLITCHTIP_REDIS_URL=redis://valkey:6379/1
# Langfuse — LLM traces: model, tokens, cost, cache hit, verdicts (§22).
# PUBLIC/SECRET keys are optional @studio/config rows (worker schema);
# LANGFUSE_HOST is read by packages/agent/src/obs/langfuse.ts (cloud default
# https://cloud.langfuse.com; self-host only after ~100 users or a privacy
# requirement, §17.2 — it is heavy). Prompts stay masked until then.
LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=changeme-pk
LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=changeme-sk
# LANGFUSE_HOST=https://cloud.langfuse.com
# METRICS_TOKEN — shared secret for the internal Prometheus-format /metrics
# endpoints (gateway + worker): HTTP Basic auth, username ignored, compared
# timing-safe; UNSET = the endpoint FAILS CLOSED (401). Also interpolated
# into the Prometheus container by infra/compose (obs profile). Internal
# network only — never behind a public route.
METRICS_TOKEN=changeme

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Email — transactional only: invites, receipts, run finished (§17.1)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# future: no code parses these yet (email wave); kept as the agreed contract —
# Resend first, swap to Amazon SES via a provider adapter if volume grows.
# RESEND_API_KEY=changeme
# EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=no-reply@changeme.example

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deploy / CI knobs (documented in full in infra/environments.md — the box
# .env may also carry these; apps never parse them)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMAGE_TAG, GATEWAY_IMAGE, WORKER_IMAGE, ENGINE_POOL_IMAGE, WEB_IMAGE (GHCR
# refs / git-sha tags), ENGINE_PIN (ADR-0001 engine commit pre-flight),
# ALLOW_LATEST + PREV_IMAGE_TAG + STATE_DIR + BUILD_ON_BOX + ROLLBACK_YES
# (deploy-v2.sh / rollback.sh), COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME + ENV_FILE (staging
# separation, §17.5), WORKER_HEALTH_URL, SMOKE_BASE_URL, SMOKE_TIMEOUT,
# ENGINE_SMOKE_CMD (smoke.sh), LICENSE_CHECK_STRICT (scripts/check-licenses).
